      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 6</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The organization has members, who are primarily parents, teachers, and community supporters, as described in its bylaws. Members support the organization's mission through participation in meetings, voting in elections for officers, and engaging in sponsored activities. The organization does not have stockholders.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 7a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The members of the PTA (parents and school staff) elect the Board of Directors, including the President, Treasurer, and other officers. Certain governance decisions, including budget approval and policy adoption, are subject to approval via general membership meetings in accordance with PTA bylaws.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 7b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Certain governance decisions, such as the election of officers, approval of the annual budget, and amendments to the standing rules, are reserved to the general membership. These decisions are made by members in accordance with the organization's bylaws during regular or special meetings.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The Form 990 was prepared by the Treasurer and reviewed with other officers including the President prior to filing. Board members receive a copy for review before submission.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Reviewed annually. Conflict policy located here (from California PTA): https://toolkit.capta.org/running-your-pta/planning-organizing/conflict-of-interest-policy/</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The organization makes its governing documents, conflict of interest policy, and financial statements available upon request as required by law. Most policies/bylaws are available on the CA PTA website. Requests may be submitted to the PTA Treasurer directly, or any other executive board member, who will forward the request to the PTA Treasurer.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VIII, Line 1a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Revenue from donation-based campaigns such as the Friends and Family Giving Campaign and Read-A-Thon was reported under Part VIII, Line 1 as contributions. No goods or services were provided in exchange for these donations. Fundraising events reported on Line 8 include only raffles and similar events where tickets are sold</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part XI, Line 9</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>An adjustment was entered on this line to reconcile the difference between total net assets as calculated from current-year revenue and expenses and total net assets per the balance sheet in Part X. The difference arises from the treatment of certain items (including net tracking of merchandise inventory and related fees) as well as the impact of two checks totaling $2,975.55 written in late 2023 that cleared cash in 2024. The checks reduced the 2024 beginning cash balance but are not included in current year expenses. This adjustment does not represent additional income or expense beyond what is reported in Parts VII and IX for the year, but ensures that Part XI and Part X reconcile.</ExplanationTxt>
